{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Preflight Before Script Run",
  "description": "When an experiment runner or analysis script is created or edited, automatically run preflight validation to catch data leakage, regime violations, descending sweep errors, and configuration issues before execution.",
  "version": "3.0.0",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "scripts/experiment_runners/run_*.py",
      "scripts/experiment_runners/verify_*.py",
      "analysis/run_*.py",
      "analysis/step*.py",
      "experiments/*/exp_*.py"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A script that may define experiment variants was just edited. Determine if it contains variant definitions by checking for: (1) build_noiseless_variants / build_noisy_variants / build_extended_variants functions (standard VariantRunner pattern), or (2) a VARIANTS list (legacy pattern), or (3) PipelineVariant imports. \n\nIf the script defines variants:\n  Run: `.venv/bin/python scripts/preflight.py --from-script <path_to_edited_file>`\n  - If exit code = 1 (ERRORS): Report the errors to the user. Do NOT execute the script until errors are resolved.\n  - If exit code = 0 (clean or warnings only): Note any warnings. The script is safe to execute when requested.\n\nIf the script does NOT define variants (e.g., it's a standalone analysis, a scan tool, or a diagnostic script without PipelineVariant definitions):\n  Skip preflight — it only validates variant configurations. Simply note that the file was edited and proceed normally.\n\nKey: preflight.py uses --from-script which dynamically imports the module and calls the build_*_variants() functions. It will fail gracefully if the script doesn't follow the variant runner pattern."
  }
}
